Z||000000||ig88vsbobafett||11-27-2001||12:12 PM||||I am leaking oil out the frount of my moter 2.5 fiero i cant find where its comming out i know its not the valve cover (I think its hitting the belt cuzz it all over my batery)<BR>Any hints on where it could be comming from i just bought it a week ago||||reg||1
Z||000001||FieroJoe||11-27-2001||01:17 PM||||How do you know it is not the valve cover?  If it is near where it could get on the battery that's one of the only places it would be coming out.  Is it the oil fill cap?  The seals on the bottoms of those can get worn and not seal very well.<BR>The pushrod/lifter cover under the intake manifold could be another one...||||reg||1
Z||000002||fierospeeder||11-27-2001||02:50 PM||||its usually on the front oilpan where it meets the timing cover.<P><BR>You better watch your belt.  The oil is going to corrode the belt and it will break on you.   <P><P>------------------<BR>Fiero Technician<P>74 Vw Beetle<BR>83 Honda Nighthawk 550<BR>84 Pontiac Fiero<BR>87 Ford Thunderbird Turbo<P>Selling a car is like giving your own kid for adoption.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Jake_Dragon||11-27-2001||06:24 PM||||Check the seal in the timing cover.<BR>Mine leaks about a quart a month.<BR>Before anyone yells it is parked till I can get it fixed.||||reg||1
